WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.936
-My first guest tonight is
an Emmy-nominated actor.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.237
Man, he hits it out of the park.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.739
You can see him
on "This Is Us,"

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.675
which airs Tuesdays at 9:00 P.M.
on NBC.

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.210
Here is Milo Ventimiglia,
everybody.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.945
Yo!
-What's up, Jimmy?

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.079
What's up, man?

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:15.815
-Milo, it is great
to see you, pal.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.149
Thank you so much for coming
on the show.

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:19.185
-I know, through all
the ones and zeros, man.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.754
That's how we do it these days.
-It's unbelievable, right?

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.723
Are you on set right now?
-Yeah.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.125
No, I'm in my office
in Los Angeles.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.927
-Okay.
-But the studio, Paramount,

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.495
where we film,
is like a block away.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.998
-Do you film at Paramount?
I did not know that.

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.766
-Yeah, we're at Paramount.
We are, man.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:36.402
-That's where Lorne hired me
for "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.904
-No, really?
-Out in the lot, in his -- yeah,

00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:40.606
he had an office on the lot.
-By the way,

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.142
that was such an
incredible audition tape.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:46.011
I watched it. It popped up,
you know, in my thought.

00:00:46.011 --> 00:00:48.181
I watched not like
three weeks ago.

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:49.715
-No.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:51.183
-Oh, my God.
It's so embarrassing.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.652
-It was incredible.
-No.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.920
-It's not -- it's not
embarrassing.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.455
That's like -- that's like
early days.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.922
That's salad days, man.
That's good stuff.

00:00:56.922 --> 00:00:58.624
-I mean, that was like --
I wore the tightest clothes

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.293
I've ever seen in my --
I don't know.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.995
I think I was like auditioning
for Cirque du Soleil

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.496
or something.
I was something --

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.931
I was like --
-Yeah, but it was also --

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:07.700
it was the '90s, right?
-Yeah. Yeah, like 2000.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.169
-Yeah.
-Yeah, late '90s, '98.

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.438
-Late '90s, yeah.
So that was the transition

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:15.008
going out of the grunge into --
-Yes.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.042
-Yeah. I remember.
-And you know, weirdly enough,

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:19.745
I based my haircut
on a photoshoot I saw

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:22.148
in a magazine
of Kate Beckinsale.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:26.485
She had -- she cut her spikey
and short for some movie

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:28.755
and I thought she looked
so cool, and I was like,

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.456
"I'm gonna do that haircut."
It's so dumb,

00:01:30.456 --> 00:01:32.391
but it's the truth.
-That's incredible.

00:01:32.391 --> 00:01:34.226
-Isn't that weird?
-That's amazing.

00:01:34.226 --> 00:01:35.795
-I had so many fads --
-Yeah.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.230
-...of hairstyles and
ridiculousness.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.066
But I love Paramount so much.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.701
-Milo, I got to talk to you
about this 'cause you did

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.770
something that --
I love that you do what you say.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:46.439
You said, "Dude, I'm gonna get
an Airstream.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.641
I'm gonna like travel,"
and I go, "Love it, man.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.243
I can't wait."
But you did.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.610
You bought an Airstream.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:52.946
-And you drove it around
the U.S.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.546
I want to know every single
detail.

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:56.982
I want to know everything.
Look at this thing.

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:59.886
I love Airstreams.
-Yeah.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.288
I mean, listen man, Airstreams
are sexy.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.756
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.426
But I also realize it's kind of
luxury premier item.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.828
So I call it my camper.
-Yeah, okay.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.329
-I call it my camper.
-Yeah.

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:12.531
-'Cause it feels like it brings
me down to Earth a little bit.

00:02:12.531 --> 00:02:14.934
-You -- it is.
-But, yeah, so --

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.503
Yeah, I think so.
I mean, you know, you're driving

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:19.939
around and you got this big
silver bullet behind you,

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.807
and it's sexy and it's cool
and, you know,

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:24.977
you can stop on a hillside
and you take a photo

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.613
and it's just incredible.

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.448
You know, vistas and everything.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.384
But like the real truth is,
you're driving hours and hours

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.953
and hours and hours, and when
you're done driving 13 hours,

00:02:34.953 --> 00:02:37.523
you got to hook up and line
and pump your own crap.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.559
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:40.960
That's the part they don't
advertise.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.729
-That's what's -- that's not
in the brochure.

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:46.532
-[ Laughs ]
But I mean, isn't it great

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:49.101
like when it rains
on an Airstream

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:52.338
and the tap of the rain
on the tin of the --

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.839
You can't --
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:58.044
I mean, it's -- listen, it is --
it is a travel like none other.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.045
-I'd love to do it.
-And I'd always wanted to do it.

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:01.680
I know we talked about it.
-Me too.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.516
-And so I did it.
Like, you know, quarantine

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.085
happened, and what was going on
in the world

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:09.255
was going on in the world, and I
wanted to go see my sisters.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.024
One was in Utah and another one
is up in Oregon.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:14.460
And as I was going through,
I was like

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.630
really researching this,
and I was trying to find a spot

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.666
where I could pick one up
along the way.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.135
You know, I had my truck,
so I was good.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.437
And then when I --
I brokered a deal

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.071
with a dealer up in Oregon.

00:03:26.071 --> 00:03:27.373
So I bought it in Oregon,

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.775
and then I drove it
back down to L.A.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.743
and then I drove across
to Georgia,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.679
and then all the way back.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.381
That's the dream.
That's the dream, dude.

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:36.715
-Yeah.
-That's something

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:38.551
I think about doing,
and I don't know if I'll ever,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.486
I mean, have the chance
to do it, really.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.155
Just awesome.
-Well, you know what you

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:46.125
ought to do is, you fly out
somewhere where I'm gonna be.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.828
We'll hang out, we'll drive
around the block,

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.330
and I'll drop you off
at the airport

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.065
so you get the experience of it,

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.800
but you don't have to worry
about pumping your own stuff.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.202
-That's my man.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.937
See, that's what friends
are for, bud.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.072
-Yeah.
-I want to get to "This Is Us,"

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.907
and I want to talk to you
about the new season.

00:04:01.907 --> 00:04:04.544
But during the pandemic,
people have been binge-watching

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:08.547
every show they can, and you've
been on TV for many years.

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:12.918
And my first debut with you was
"Gilmore Girls" and, you know.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:14.387
-Mm-hmm.
-But can you tell

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:17.090
when people are binge-watching
one of your shows?

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:18.924
-Oh, yeah.
I mean, usually, you know,

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:21.627
social media will kind of
light up and you can tell

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:24.730
where the show was being
released and at what moment.

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:29.268
Like, toward the end of
quarantine it became evident

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:32.805
that we had a new season down
in Argentina, in Brazil.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.574
So, you know, you see the
messages and people popping up.

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.676
-That's great.
-And then recently, I think now

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:39.946
they're cycling back through
it in Italy.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.013
-Wow.

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.515
-And like seeing
what's going on.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.350
Back in Europe, you're like,
oh, you guys are back indoors.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.686
You're not out, you know, having
a pizza and coffee anymore.

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:47.920
-Yeah.
-I get it. I get it.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.690
-Yeah, but I love that
you get to entertain.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.424
It's global now.
You know, it used to be

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:53.860
just an American thing --
-Yeah.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.863
-...American TV, and now
it's worldwide.

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.531
That's pretty cool.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:05:00.866
Yeah, I mean, you know, and the
Pearsons are absolutely kind of,

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:03.269
you know, America's family
in a way.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:07.206
But really what I see
most still -- still --

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:09.742
is people going back
and watching "Gilmore Girls."

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.410
It always goes back to Jess.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.878
Always goes back to Jess.
-I'm Team Jess.

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:14.447
Day one, Team Jess.
-I know you are.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:15.815
-Yeah, have to be.
-I know.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:16.949
-Absolutely, buddy.
-Yeah.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.651
-Oh, I love that.
I love that.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.453
-Yeah.
-It's interesting that you play,

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:23.823
like, the bad boy and then you
play Jack who is the --

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:26.259
probably the best dude on Earth.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:28.227
He's the nice --
-He's one of them, man.

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.662
-He's one of the good guys.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.196
-Yeah, he's one of
the good guys.

00:05:31.196 --> 00:05:32.598
But I mean, I'll tell you what,

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:35.033
those are hard shoes
to fill at times.

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:36.569
-[ Laughs ] Exactly.
-You know?

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:40.906
I've had moments in life where
people expect me to be Jack.

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:44.577
And like, you know, I'll be
honest, I mean, I think Jack

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:47.547
borrows from Milo
and Milo borrows from Jack.

00:05:47.547 --> 00:05:49.382
Or Milo gets the benefit of

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.851
wearing the Jack face
all the time.

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:54.787
But man, it's tough living up
to it sometimes.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.089
It really is.
If you notice like sometimes

00:05:57.089 --> 00:05:59.792
when I do a lot of press,
I'll talk about Jack's flaws

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:03.028
just to humanize myself
a little bit.

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:05.231
To kind of let myself off
the hook a little.

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:08.367
-Yeah. No, yeah, but if you
are any way in a bad mood,

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.903
you should be like --
[ Deep breathing ]

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.905
"You got to be Jack right now."
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.073
-"Hey, Dad, you mind --"
blah blah blah.

00:06:15.073 --> 00:06:16.742
You can't have a freak out.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:18.176
-'Cause like,
"Jack doesn't do that."

00:06:18.176 --> 00:06:20.546
-You're like, listen,
I just -- I just pumped

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:24.316
my own crap from an Airstream,
sure, but yeah, hi. Hi.

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:26.418
-Behind the scenes over at
"This Is Us," you guys have

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:29.922
a reason to celebrate because
your co-star, one of our favs,

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.691
Mandy Moore is pregnant.
-Mm-hmm. Yeah.

00:06:32.691 --> 00:06:34.026
Yeah, she is.
-Were you all back at work

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.594
when you found out?
Where were you?

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.029
-No, no, we weren't.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:40.532
So over the course of
quarantine, we had, as a cast,

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:42.335
as a group, FaceTimed
with one --

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:46.272
or had a big Zoom together
and we kept up,

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.806
made sure everyone was okay.

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:52.478
But then, as we were getting
ready to film, we had a Zoom

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:55.047
with Fogelman, where Fogelman
was actually kind of giving us

00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:57.282
the lay of the land, what the
protocols were looking like,

00:06:57.282 --> 00:06:59.318
and if anybody was going to be
uncomfortable with them,

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.721
like speak up
or hold your peace.

00:07:01.721 --> 00:07:05.391
And then he hopped off and we
were all going around, like,

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:08.127
"Hey, Sterling, you good?
Hey, Chrissy, Justin,

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:10.162
like everyone feels good?
Yeah, I feel good about it.

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.097
Mandy?"
And Mandy wasn't talking.

00:07:12.097 --> 00:07:16.002
She wasn't talking.
And then she just kind of goes,

00:07:16.002 --> 00:07:18.037
"Well, guys, I am pregnant."

00:07:18.037 --> 00:07:20.606
And I mean, then,
you know, we're --

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:22.308
-Crying.
-Exactly.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.610
Exactly, man.
Crying, excited.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:29.214
You know. And --
I mean, she's the loveliest,

00:07:29.214 --> 00:07:32.718
she's great, she's amazing,
and, like, to know that

00:07:32.718 --> 00:07:35.954
a human being like Mandy Moore
is going to be a mom

00:07:35.954 --> 00:07:37.957
influencing a child
in this Earth

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:39.858
just gives me hope for Earth.

00:07:39.858 --> 00:07:41.761
-[ Laughs and applauds ]

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:46.098
I want to talk about this part
of "This Is Us."

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:50.303
This season that was hinted
how Rebecca and Miguel

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:53.973
got together after Jack died.
-Yeah.

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:56.208
-Now we might find out a little
more to that relationship.

00:07:56.208 --> 00:08:00.379
But as Jack, how do you feel
about that relationship?

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:01.814
-Jack's dead.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:04.116
So it doesn't really matter
what Jack thinks.

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:07.587
I mean, let's be glaringly
honest.

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:09.956
-Yes.
-You know, I think -- listen,

00:08:09.956 --> 00:08:12.624
Jack -- Jack loves his wife.

00:08:12.624 --> 00:08:15.594
He loves his kids like no other.
-Yep.

00:08:15.594 --> 00:08:18.564
-But at the same time,
you know, Jack wouldn't want

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:22.835
his wife or kids to be
unhappy without him.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.603
And, you know, I mean, look,

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:26.906
death is a pretty great
equalizer.

00:08:26.906 --> 00:08:30.509
When someone dies, like, yeah,
I guess that's kind of over.

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:35.381
So it's not like Miguel got in
the way of Jack and Rebecca.

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:38.917
It was just, hey,
Rebecca was available.

00:08:38.917 --> 00:08:40.519
-Yeah.
-And they had a history

00:08:40.519 --> 00:08:42.021
of being close and friends,

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:44.656
and everything should start
with the friendship.

00:08:44.656 --> 00:08:46.425
-Yeah, I agree with that,
by the way.

00:08:46.425 --> 00:08:47.560
-Yeah.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:49.194
-My wife and I started,
best friends.

00:08:49.194 --> 00:08:51.163
We were just friends.
Loved hanging out.

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:52.665
It was awesome.
I agree with that.

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:54.567
-And then before we did
the interview,

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:56.034
you gave me your
wife's phone number.

00:08:56.034 --> 00:08:57.670
So, oh boy.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.438
-Dude, I'm so
embarrassed about that.

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.139
We'll have to talk about that
next time you're on.

00:09:01.139 --> 00:09:03.008
But I --
-We have to, man.

00:09:03.008 --> 00:09:04.810
That's incredible.
It's incredible.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.311
[ Laughter ]
-I can't believe it.

00:09:06.311 --> 00:09:07.913
-For anybody --
-Did she text you back?

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:10.783
-Yeah, long story short,
I was -- hold on, let me see.

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:12.484
I was trying to text Jimmy
something --

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:13.618
Hey, there it is.

00:09:13.618 --> 00:09:15.521
She wrote, "This is incredible.

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:17.289
I will send to him
immediately."

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:19.124
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:19.124 --> 00:09:21.493
I'm sorry, dude. I thought
I was giving you my number.

00:09:21.493 --> 00:09:23.829
I don't know my number.
That's insane.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:26.798
-That's great. That's great.
-That's totally real and insane.

00:09:26.798 --> 00:09:28.433
Dude, you're the best.
-I love it.

00:09:28.433 --> 00:09:32.437
-Milo -- I gave Milo Ventimiglia
my wife's phone number.

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:34.840
What am I thinking?
Milo, I love you, buddy.

